---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Pathway from '@/components/home/Pathway.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Behavior Analysis–Informed Digital Design | Juan Lopez"
  description="A behavior-analytic, evidence-informed approach to research and digital systems grounded in clarity, dignity, autonomy, and meaningful outcomes."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-shell page-hero__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
      <h1>Evidence with humility. Structure with care.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">
        I study how environments and information affect what people can understand and accomplish. The goal is not to control people. It is to remove avoidable barriers and make choices easier to see.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="page-shell principles-grid">
      <article class="principle-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">01</p>
        <h2>Everyday language first</h2>
        <p>Technical vocabulary is useful only when it makes the reasoning more precise. People should not need a glossary to understand the point.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">02</p>
        <h2>Context matters</h2>
        <p>A pattern is interpreted alongside the environment, the task, and the individual—not as a detached number.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">03</p>
        <h2>Meaningful outcomes</h2>
        <p>Measurement should return to what a person or team can do, understand, and choose in the real setting.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <header class="section-intro section-intro--center">
        <p class="eyebrow">ABA-Informed Design Pathway</p>
        <h2>Five translations from research to practice.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro__body">Each step connects an everyday need to a restrained behavioral concept and a practical design implication.</p>
      </header>
      <Pathway />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="page-shell research-index-card">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Ethical foundation</p>
        <h2>Autonomy and dignity are part of the method.</h2>
        <p>
          Behavior analysis is strongest when socially meaningful goals, informed choice, compassion, and respect are treated as requirements. In digital work, that means avoiding deceptive pressure, making outcomes understandable, and allowing people to change their minds.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="research-index-card__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Primary sources</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1311293/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wolf (1978): social validity</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7900359/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stimulus control research and practice</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4893031/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Prompting and fading research</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.bacb.com/wp-content/ethics-code-for-behavior-analysts/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BACB Ethics Code for Behavior Analysts</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1286071/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Baer, Wolf, and Risley: dimensions revisited</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
